WEBVTT

00:36:58.746 --> 00:37:01.496
But if we get there, I think there's
a lot of scenarios in

00:37:01.496 --> 00:37:05.038
the direction that you are describing
that are worrisome.

00:37:05.038 --> 00:37:07.663
And we would want to spend a
lot of effort planning for.

00:37:09.121 --> 00:37:13.288
I mean, the fact that a computer could
start editing its own code

00:37:13.288 --> 00:37:17.288
and improving itself while we're asleep
and you wake up in the morning

00:37:17.288 --> 00:37:21.246
and it's got smarter, that is the start
of something super powerful

00:37:21.246 --> 00:37:22.746
and potentially scary.

00:37:24.454 --> 00:37:29.413
I have tremendous misgivings about letting
my system, not one we have today,

00:37:29.413 --> 00:37:30.496
but one that we might not have